# Next.js App Router

## Structure

- Use App Router under `client/app/`
- Route groups: `(app)` for shell pages, `(auth)` for public auth
- Shared UI in `client/components/`; API helpers in `client/lib/apiUtils.ts`
- Navigation lives in `client/components/AppNav.tsx`

## Components

```tsx
// ✅ Client interactivity
"use client";

// ✅ Server Component by default when no hooks/browser APIs are needed
export default function Page() {
  return <h1>Home</h1>;
}
```

- Add `"use client"` only when using hooks, events, or browser APIs
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation
- Fetch via `apiGet` / `apiPost` / `apiPut` / `apiDelete` from `@/lib/apiUtils`
- Keep pages focused; extract modals/forms into `components/`
- Follow `.cursor/rules/page-navigation.mdc`: breadcrumbs on pages; action forms **Cancel** then **Save**

## Do not

- Import from outside `client/` for UI modules (except documented shared paths)
- Hardcode `http://localhost:5000` for API calls
- Put secrets in client code (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*` only for non-secret config)
